WEBVTT

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:13.240
Me first!

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:16.860
Darn it, Nanana!
 When we get back, I'm gonna kill you!

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.660
<i>Nothing gets me excited like an adventure.</i>

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.220
<i>An inquisitive spirit,
 ambition, and dreams to pursue...</i>

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:30.760
<i>I think everybody needs
 that to make life worth living.</i>

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.190
Ow, hot!

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:34.170
<i>But modern society is so terribly dull</i>

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:38.170
<i>that a lot of kids never know what 
it's like to feel their hearts race.</i>

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.170
Sorry, Sansa!

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.280
<i>While I was eating pudding earlier, 
I came up with a great idea.</i>

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.270
<i>I just had to make it myself!</i>

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.150
<i>A place filled with
 laughter and puzzles to solve,</i>

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.100
<i>for young people with adventurous hearts.</i>

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:28.380
I'm...

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:34.460
Free!

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:10.570
<i>Nanae Island is a manmade 
island in the Pacific Ocean.</i>

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.460
<i>Also known as the
 Special Student Zone, Nanae Island</i>

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:20.240
<i>was created to house students,
 who make up most of its population.</i>

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:24.160
<i>It has 21 schools, including middle 
schools, high schools, and colleges,</i>

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.890
<i>and the courses offered 
number five times that.</i>

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:30.050
<i>It's fully equipped with
 facilities for all sorts of training,</i>

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:33.030
<i>in addition to
 state-of-the-art research facilities.</i>

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.650
<i>But most of all...</i>

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.370
<i>It's my chance to say goodbye to that house!</i>

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:42.560
<i>Starting today, I live on 
my own and do things my way!</i>

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:51.320
<b><u>Episode 1:</u></b>

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:51.320
Disowned and Exiled

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.020
Yeah?

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:03.760
I'm the owner and manager of 
the Happy House, Maboro Shiki.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:04.970
Nice to meet you.

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:06.650
I'm Yama Juugo.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:08.930
Pleased to meet you.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.730
So, how old are you, Juugo?

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.070
Sixteen.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:21.880
I'll start my third year of high 
school the day after tomorrow.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:23.890
May of your second year

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:26.820
is a pretty awkward 
time to change schools.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:31.610
Yeah, well... my dad sort of exiled me.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:33.560
Yeah? That's interesting.

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:36.040
He's a jackass.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:41.790
Oh, yeah. The real estate agent 
told you about our terms, right?

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:42.590
Yes.

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:45.320
One room plus kitchen, 
bath and toilet separate.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:49.350
Furnished with appliances and
 extras for just 5,000 yen per month.

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:52.140
But you pay one year's 
worth of rent in advance,

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.600
and there are no refunds, 
under any circumstances.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:55.400
That okay?

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:56.440
Yes.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:58.950
I look forward to living here.

00:04:58.950 --> 00:04:59.980
Sure.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:05.950
Okay, I'll show you to your room.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:07.450
Happy House

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:07.450
Oh... Okay.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.930
You'll be in room 202.

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:23.010
Here you go. Use it as you please.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:26.470
<i>What? The key? Use it how?</i>

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:26.470
Go in and check it out.

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:58.790
Sorry! Wrong room!

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:04.510
Um, there's someone in there!

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.760
What? No one lives here.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:10.470
See? Someone's here!

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:15.170
I told you, there are no people living here.

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:16.220
No, no, no!

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:17.470
That girl!

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:18.420
What girl?

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:19.370
Her!

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:21.110
Oh, she's different.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:25.370
That's the ghost of a girl who was 
murdered in here about ten years ago.

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:27.120
What?!

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:29.460
Aww, you spilled the beans just like that?

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:30.780
A ghost?

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:33.110
Whether you believe it or not is up to you,

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:35.740
but I did tell you it
 would include extras.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:37.610
Well, you've given me your rent.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:41.040
You can move out anytime you want.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:42.420
See ya.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:43.960
Wait! What are you saying?!

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:48.800
<i>I don't have the money to move out.</i>

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:54.710
Why don't you sit down?

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:02.690
What's your name?

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.400
Yama Juugo.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.620
I'm Ryuugajou Nanana.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.110
Nice to meet you.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:10.940
Ryuugajou-san, you're...

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:12.300
Call me Nanana.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:18.000
Um... Nanana-chan, you're... a ghost 
who was murdered in this room?

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:18.920
Yeah!

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:22.120
I don't know who killed me, though. 
I was stabbed from behind.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:24.640
Oh, is that right?

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:27.470
Could I, like, shake your hand?

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:28.840
Yeah, sure.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:37.930
Is this a trick?!

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:40.750
I'm the real deal!

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:46.050
Well? Satisfied now?

00:07:49.730 --> 00:07:50.610
Seriously?

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:52.980
So, again, nice to meet you!

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:59.080
Anyway, now that you understand
 that I'm a ghost bound to this room,

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:02.290
I'd like to begin the battle right away.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:03.870
Huh? Battle?

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.340
It's basically no-holds-barred.

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:08.980
You win if you get your 
opponent to admit defeat.

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:10.800
No, no... Why?

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:14.250
We should make it clear 
right away which one of us

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:16.260
is the master of this room, right?

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.870
Make it clear?

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:20.810
You won't leave this room?

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:24.980
I can't leave. I'm bound to this room.

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:27.570
You won't, like, move on?

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:29.230
I can't. That's why I'm here.

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:31.900
Then what would it take for you to move on?

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.840
Maybe if I found my
 murderer and killed him myself?

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:39.240
What the hell? That's scary.

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:42.160
I'll do something about it for you, then.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.940
So can we call off the fight for now?

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:47.880
Look, that's not the point here.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:53.010
I spend every day
 eating pudding, watching TV,

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.150
and playing online games.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:54.970
A ghost does that?

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:57.070
I told you, I'm bound here!

00:08:57.070 --> 00:09:01.130
And I have no intention of 
changing my lifestyle now.

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:04.270
So the question is,
 what are you going to do?

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:06.960
So the main resident can do as they please,

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:08.980
and the sub just has to deal with it?

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:09.610
Right.

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:14.070
So if you win,
 I'll disappear and keep quiet.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:15.900
Like that.

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:19.620
You can do stuff like that, too?

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:22.420
You don't seem too surprised.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:26.270
Well, personally, more than a battle,

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:29.440
I kind of envision a life 
of lovey-dovey cohabitation.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:36.440
If you win, I'm willing to
 pretend I'm your live-in girlfriend.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:38.270
I'm in!

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:42.940
Now it's my turn!

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:52.020
<i>Crap! It's all over!</i>

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:53.620
Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:55.030
Well? Give up,
 or I'll dislocate your shoulder!

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:57.240
<i>She's strong!</i>

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:02.410
<i>I just realized...
 My hand is in God's territory!</i>

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:05.620
<i>I can't enjoy this with the back of my hand!</i>

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:08.080
<i>If I can get just one finger... 
Just for one second...</i>

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:10.960
You can't break free! Just surrender already!

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:12.770
<i>If it's come to this,</i>

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:14.530
<i>I'll have to use the milliseconds</i>

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:17.790
<i>when my wrist will go slack at 
the moment my shoulder is broken!</i>

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:22.210
<i>My left arm in
 exchange for copping a feel...</i>

00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:22.810
<i>But...</i>

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:26.020
What?

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:29.980
Don't underestimate me just 
because I'm in this state, ghost!

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:32.560
Huh? What do you mean by that?

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:34.870
Dislocated shoulders hurt a lot.

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:36.820
And what of it?!

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:39.650
Oh? You've got some guts.

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:41.780
Don't blame me for what happens next!

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:45.320
I, Yama Juugo,
 will not give a ghost the satisfaction of

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:46.140
retreating,

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:46.850
groveling,

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:47.830
or second thoughts—

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:56.030
Nice to meet you all!

00:10:57.640 --> 00:11:00.930
Yumeji, show Yama around the school later.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.200
Yes, sir.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.820
I'm the class officer, Yumeji Yurika.

00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:07.350
<i>Black hair! Glasses! Class officer!</i>

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:07.350
Feel free to ask me anything.

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:09.270
<i>You're so in my strike zone, Yumeji-san!</i>

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:14.030
Um, what happened to your arm?

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:16.690
It's the price I paid to 
touch God's territory.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:17.940
I see...

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:22.620
It's really pretty.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:26.300
Have you heard of the
 master architect, Mutsumi Koma?

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:31.330
He built not only this school,
but most of Nanae Island's buildings, too.

00:11:31.530 --> 00:11:33.540
So it's true...

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:36.050
I'm really into Mutsumi Koma.

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:41.420
The things he designs almost 
seem to be alive, don't they?

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:44.860
What're you doing?

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:46.860
I-I'm sorry.

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:50.740
I write down quotes that 
sound beautiful to me.

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:52.890
Did it bother you?

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:54.980
Not at all. But why?

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:59.940
Well... I want to be a novelist.

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:02.950
Wow. You actually have a goal in mind, huh?

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:05.050
You're not going to laugh?

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:07.660
Do I look like that kind of guy?

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:09.600
No, I mean...

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:11.790
You're kind of attractive,

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:14.580
so I thought you might
 be the self-centered type.

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:17.330
I'm kind of... what?

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:22.420
K-K-Kind of... like a troublemaker!

00:12:26.230 --> 00:12:29.470
Am I really that mean-looking?

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:45.110
Juugo! This is terrible!

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.870
We're out of pudding!

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:50.020
Oh. Okay. I'll buy some tomorrow.

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:52.580
But I want some right now!

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:06.380
<i>Not needing sleep is the
 ultimate skill for an internet junkie.</i>

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:16.150
<i>Living with a ghost who's 
bound to my room isn't easy...</i>

00:13:19.140 --> 00:13:20.610
Instant ramen again?

00:13:21.010 --> 00:13:22.540
Like I can help it.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:25.400
What's with that tone?

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:26.860
Sorry.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:30.990
I'm going to the restroom.

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:43.050
My password still works?

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:45.970
<b>-Yuki-san, long time no see! 
-Been a long day, huh? 
I've gotten pretty used to student life here, too.
-Must be hot there...</b>

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:48.300
<i>It's active even on this island...</i>

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:47.510
<b>-Been a long day, huh? 
I've gotten pretty used to student life here, too.
-Must be hot there...
-Nanae Island is a pretty accommodating place.</b>

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:48.300
<b>-If only I were a little younger... (>_<)
-More than "a little," I'd say (lol)
-Well, I'm going to take it easy until I get further orders.
-Good luck, Yuki-chan (*^-^*)/</b>

00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:57.630
Hey! How long are you gonna be in there?

00:13:57.630 --> 00:13:58.980
Whoa! 8:00?!

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:00.540
I'm coming out now!

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:07.580
It's on a timer?

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:14.270
<b>Nanana Manual</b>

00:14:12.190 --> 00:14:13.810
Nanana Manual...

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:18.000
<b>Konjou Kasumi</b>

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:16.290
<i>Konjou Kasumi?</i>

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.000
<i>Is that a girl?</i>

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:28.410
<i>First, if you have no interest in Nanana,</i>

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:30.550
<i>I suggest you put this</i>

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:33.880
<i>notebook back and move
 out of room 202 immediately.</i>

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:36.180
Can't do that. No money.

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:40.340
"1: Nanana's weaknesses.

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:42.280
2: Nanana's favorite foods.

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:44.810
Nanana can only eat pudding.

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:47.030
Her favorite is Randoya Light Pudding.

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:49.430
Second is Minerva Honey Ice Pudding.

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:52.160
Third is Hot Springs Thick Pudding."

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:55.070
<i>5: About Nanana's Collection.</i>

00:14:55.070 --> 00:14:56.650
<i>I won't say much here.</i>

00:14:57.050 --> 00:15:01.130
<i>If you're interested, see the 
Adventure Club at Third High School.</i>

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:03.180
<i>Of course, even if you don't go,</i>

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:05.520
<i>they're likely to approach you themselves.</i>

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:08.280
<i>What you do then is up to you.</i>

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:10.050
Nanana's Collection?

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:19.060
That makes sense...

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:25.730
So you're finally out of there.

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:28.780
Nanana-chan, let's play a game! A game!

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.220
I'll show you my awesome techniques!

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:33.410
But you can't use your left hand.

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:35.460
A card game, then!

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:38.870
Behold my legendary Grand Millionaire skill!

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:41.550
Once again...

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:44.140
Oh. Then I'll have some instant ramen.

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:46.380
I'll get this arm better 
so I can play with—

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:48.340
Ugh! What is this?!

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:49.800
It's been two hours.

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:51.390
What a waste!

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:53.720
You should eat more nutritious food.

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:55.080
Can't! I have no money!

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:56.560
I'll just tough it out!

00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:58.770
You're weird, Juugo.

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:01.960
<i>Hey, this is easy.</i>

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:07.780
<i>Finally, if you've taken even the 
slightest interest in Nanana,</i>

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:09.940
<i>please stay by her side.</i>

00:16:10.230 --> 00:16:11.710
You're really gonna eat that?

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:13.270
<i>Other than the
 peculiarity of being a ghost,</i>

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:14.240
I can't let food go to waste!

00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:20.320
<i>Ryuugajou Nanana is the same lonely 
girl she was ten years ago.</i>

00:16:22.060 --> 00:16:23.790
<i>So, you who came after me,</i>

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:27.450
<i>please save my best friend.</i>

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:32.770
<i>"Ryuugajou Nanana.</i>

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:36.830
<i>Head of the Great 7,
 who proposed the Nanae Island Project.</i>

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:40.230
<i>But she was murdered in her own home.</i>

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:42.300
<i>Thorough investigations were conducted,</i>

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:44.480
<i>but the murderer still has not been found."</i>

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:48.780
<i>"The Nanae Island Project</i>

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:51.530
<i>refers to development of the 
then-unsettled Nanae Island</i>

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:53.730
<i>with the goal of creating a place</i>

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:56.200
<i>where young people pursue any dream.</i>

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:59.200
<i>Support was freely offered 
to ambitious students,</i>

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:04.500
<i>and the massive profits gained from 
their research was returned to the island."</i>

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:07.960
<i>Nanana-chan was that big a deal?</i>

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:13.720
<b>Ikkaku Shunjuu 
Futaba Saito 
Kurosu Sansa 
Maboro Shiki 
Kakyou Uzuki 
Mutsumi Koma 
Ryuugajou Nanana</b>

00:17:10.540 --> 00:17:12.250
<i>Maboro Shiki?</i>

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:14.930
<i>Wha?</i>

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:18.220
Hi there.

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:22.110
I'm about the fourth most important 
person on this island, Maboro Shiki.

00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:26.400
Currently seeking a boyfriend who'll let 
me drink alcohol for the rest of my life.

00:17:26.930 --> 00:17:29.770
By the way, what do you 
think about me, Juugo?

00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:31.230
No, thank you.

00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:32.360
I see.

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:37.180
So, you want to know more about Nanana?

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:38.070
Yes.

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:42.060
Juugo, didn't you find it strange

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:45.540
that seven mere students made 
Nanae Island what it is now?

00:17:45.940 --> 00:17:50.110
Isn't that because the 
Great 7 were all geniuses?

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:53.260
It's true that our plan 
was essentially flawless.

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:58.220
But we students didn't
 have any money or sponsors.

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:01.600
That's when Nanana said...

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:03.960
"I'll do something about it."

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:08.370
And then Nanana really did
 find a fortune in gold and silver

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:10.560
so we could make our dream a reality.

00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:12.420
A fortune?

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:15.280
Yep, treasures of origins unknown.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.680
Once she had the funds, Nanana traveled

00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:20.490
all over the world at every chance she got.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:23.890
See? I went with her a few times.

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:29.200
She was so cute back then.

00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:34.840
You didn't consider helping 
Nanana-chan move on?

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:37.690
Sure we did. We got an exorcist to—

00:18:37.690 --> 00:18:41.300
No, I mean, you didn't 
try to find her killer?

00:18:41.770 --> 00:18:46.480
Look, Nanana was the leader of
 this island both in name and in deed.

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:49.100
Everyone was in a frenzy 
trying to find the killer.

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:51.020
But we still hit a dead end.

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:56.100
By the way,
 why are you renting out that room?

00:18:56.580 --> 00:19:00.480
I don't want to lose money from 
a room just because of a ghost.

00:19:00.480 --> 00:19:02.650
That's out of bounds in so many ways.

00:19:02.650 --> 00:19:05.350
Plus, with someone there,

00:19:05.820 --> 00:19:07.710
she won't be so lonely.

00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:10.150
You can't stay with her?

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:13.780
I was kidding.
 Nanana doesn't need me with her.

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:16.950
Is that all?
 If there's nothing else, I'm done.

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:19.720
Oh, what's "Nanana's Collection"?

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:23.600
You know some interesting things, don't you?

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:24.350
Really...

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:29.830
Nanana's fortune, said to be worth
 hundreds of billions or even trillions of yen.

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:32.190
Also known as Ryuugajou 
Nanana's Buried Treasure.

00:19:32.990 --> 00:19:37.790
Among its riches, the ones with unique 
powers are known as Nanana's Collection.

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:39.150
Unique powers?

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:42.460
Sorta like that robot cat's secret gadgets.

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:45.220
Suddenly this all sounds pretty fake.

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:47.750
I guess. But it's true.

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:49.460
I've seen them.

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:52.980
Their locations were unknown 
when Nanana was killed,

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:56.880
but they've been found in various places 
on the island in the ten years since.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:59.550
Only a few have been found, though.

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:03.340
Many of them still lie 
somewhere on this island.

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:06.790
See? Sounds like a dream, doesn't it?

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:34.750
Well, guess I'll get going, too.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:48.150
Yes. The articles left at the scene suggest

00:20:48.150 --> 00:20:50.720
that the phantom thieves, 
Matsuri, are responsible.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:51.600
Yes.

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:54.950
D-Don't! You'll get in trouble again!

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:56.140
Hey! You can't come in here!

00:20:56.140 --> 00:20:57.390
Who do you think you are?!

00:20:58.490 --> 00:21:01.770
Me? Just a passing master detective.

00:22:33.600 --> 00:22:35.270
Thank you very much.
